{# Sign-out used to drop you straight back on the sign-in form, which reads as a failed login
   rather than a completed action - the same screen you would see if the password had been
   wrong. This says what happened, then offers the two things anyone actually wants next. #}
<section class="container mx-auto px-4 py-10 max-w-md min-h-[calc(100vh-12rem)] flex flex-col justify-center">
  <div class="card p-8 shadow-md text-center">
    <div class="mx-auto mb-5 flex h-14 w-14 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-brand-accent/10 text-brand-accent">
      {% icon "fa-solid-sign-out-alt", "text-2xl" %}
    </div>

    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-text">You are signed out</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-brand-muted">
      Your session has been ended on this device and revoked on the server, so it is closed
      everywhere you were signed in.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3">
      <a href="/login/" class="btn-primary text-center">Sign in again</a>
      <a href="https://tzortzoglou.eu/" id="leave" class="btn-secondary text-center">Back to tzortzoglou.eu</a>
    </div>

    {# WCAG 2.2.1: a time limit has to be cancellable, and the countdown has to be visible rather
       than something that simply happens to you. aria-live so it is announced, but polite and
       only on the whole sentence, not once per tick. #}
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-brand-muted">
      <span id="countdown" hidden>Returning to tzortzoglou.eu in <span id="secs">10</span> seconds.</span>
      <button type="button" id="stay" class="underline hover:text-brand-accent" hidden>Stay here</button>
    </p>
    <p id="status" class="sr-only" role="status"></p>
  </div>
</section>
